  "question": {
    "text": "If \\(f(x)=3 \\sqrt[3]{x^2}-x^2\\), then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "p7QiS",
      "text": "f has no extrema",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "uBkDH",
      "text": "\\(f\\) is maximum at two points \\(x=1\\) and \\(x=-1\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PD9V9",
      "text": "\\(f\\) is minimum at \\(x=0\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "6fXKQ",
      "text": "f has maximum at \\(x=1\\) only",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint : \\(f(x)=3(x)^{\\frac{2}{3}}-x^2\\)\nDifferentiate both sides wrt. \\(x\\)\n\\(=f^{\\prime}(x)=3 \\cdot \\frac{2}{3} x^{-1 / 3}-2 x=2 x^{-1 / 3}-2 x=2\\left(x^{-1 / 3}-x\\right)=2\\left(\\frac{1-x^{4 / 3}}{x^{1 / 3}}\\right)\\)\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/oAnN5fWzxsCSngTk_4Gsfkzbhg3PIgMCaeGxhDMJnBU.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n\\(\\therefore f\\) has maximum at two points \\(x=-1 x=1\\)\n\\(f\\) has minimum at \\(x=0\\)",
    "image": null
  },
